    {
      "id": "story-001",
      "title": "Miller's Amazing Day",
      "titleZh": "Miller 奇妙的一天",
      "intro": "On the **way** to the playground, Miller wears a silly **dress** and plays **tag** and **hide-and-seek**. His friends **pick up** the **rest** of the **balloons** and **add** them to their toy **trucks**.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "title": "The playground",
          "image": "case001.jpeg",
          "english": "On the **way** to the playground, Miller wears a silly **dress** and plays **tag** and **hide-and-seek**. His friends **pick up** the **rest** of the **balloons** and **add** them to their toy **trucks**.\n\nThey ran **near** the **slides**, balanced on the **boards**, and shot **hoops**.",
          "translation": "",
          "labels": "",
          "days": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "title": "The clown show",
          "image": "case002.jpeg",
          "english": "**Far** across the room, a **bat** began to **glide** **near** a fish **tank** under a bright **ray** of light.\n\nA **clown** in a funny **costume** began to **juggle**. He decided to **show** us a silly **act**, and then he took a **bow**.",
          "translation": "",
          "labels": "",
          "days": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "title": "The beach workshop",
          "image": "case003.jpeg",
          "english": "At the beach, the children use **science** to **dig** for **shells** and **build** sand **castles**.\n\nThey **build** a monster from **wood**, **stone**, and **metal**, tie it with **rope**, and place it beside the castles. Their newly **built** monster looks funny but friendly.",
          "translation": "",
          "labels": "",
          "days": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "title": "Baking and making",
          "image": "case004.jpeg",
          "english": "By **myself**, I **mix** **flour** and **butter** near the **oven**, then **roll** out the dough and **fold** it over.\n\nFinally, I **tear** a sheet of paper, **fold** it into a box, and use **glue** and **tape** to hold it together.",
          "translation": "",
          "labels": "",
          "days": ""
        }
      ],
      "week": 1,
      "startDay": 1,
      "endDay": 8,
      "entryCount": 45,
      "sceneCount": 4,
      "cover": "case001.jpeg",
      "coverAlt": "The playground",
      "hasPdf": true
    },
    {
      "id": "story-002",
      "title": "Miller's Busy Saturday",
      "titleZh": "Miller 忙碌的星期六",
      "intro": "Miller gave Grandma a **hug** before helping her **bake** a pie.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "title": "A kitchen hug",
          "image": "story-002-scene-01.png",
          "english": "Miller gave Grandma a **hug** before helping her **bake** a pie.\n\nThey put **broccoli** and **cabbage** in the pie.\n\nThere was a **chile pepper** beside the **corn** and **lettuce** on the table.",
          "translation": "Miller 抱了抱奶奶，然后帮她烤馅饼。馅饼里放了西兰花和甘蓝菜，桌上还有辣椒、玉米和生菜。",
          "labels": "hug, bake, broccoli, cabbage, chile pepper, corn, lettuce.",
          "days": "Day 9"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "title": "Coins and a nature poster",
          "image": "story-002-scene-02.png",
          "english": "In Grandma's coin box, Miller found a **penny**, a **nickel**, and a **dime**.\n\nOn a nature poster, a fish had shiny **scales**, a bird had a soft **feather**, and a porcupine had sharp **spines**.\n\nA turtle's shell looked like **armor**, covering the soft **skin** underneath.",
          "translation": "Miller 在奶奶的硬币盒里找到了三种硬币。动物海报上的鱼鳞闪闪发亮，鸟有柔软的羽毛，豪猪有尖刺。乌龟的壳像盔甲，保护着下面柔软的皮肤。",
          "labels": "penny, nickel, dime, scales, feather, spines, armor, skin.",
          "days": "Day 10"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "title": "A pretend parade",
          "image": "story-002-scene-03.png",
          "english": "Miller **joined** a pretend **army**, and the **soldiers** **marched** in a **parade**.\n\nThe **corporal** and **sergeant** wore **stripes** on their sleeves and **kept** in **step**.\n\n**Nobody** **wanted** to stop, but it was time for a snack **instead**.",
          "translation": "Miller 加入了扮演军队的游戏，大家扮成士兵参加游行。下士和军士的袖子上有条纹，他们步伐一致。虽然没人想停下来，但大家该改为吃点心了。",
          "labels": "joined, army, soldiers, marched, parade, corporal, sergeant, stripes, kept, step, Nobody, wanted, instead.",
          "days": "Day 11"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "title": "A boat on the lid",
          "image": "story-002-scene-04.png",
          "english": "Back home, Miller **fed** the ducks and **dried** his hands.\n\nThen he **ran** to the toy **bin**.\n\nA little boat sat on **top** of the bin's **lid**.",
          "translation": "回到家，Miller 喂了鸭子并擦干双手。他跑到玩具箱旁，发现一只小船放在箱子盖的上面。",
          "labels": "fed, dried, ran, bin, top, lid.",
          "days": "Day 12、Day 13"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "title": "The little raft",
          "image": "story-002-scene-05.png",
          "english": "Miller took his toy **raft** to a little stream.\n\nHe **slid** it into the water, but a twig on the raft **broke**.\n\nGrandma helped him fix it, and the raft floated again.",
          "translation": "Miller 带着玩具木筏来到小溪边，把它轻轻滑入水中。木筏上的小树枝断了，奶奶帮忙修好后，它又漂了起来。",
          "labels": "raft, slid, broke.",
          "days": "Day 14"
        }
      ],
      "week": 2,
      "startDay": 9,
      "endDay": 14,
      "entryCount": 37,
      "sceneCount": 5,
      "cover": "story-002-scene-01.png",
      "coverAlt": "A kitchen hug",
      "hasPdf": false
    },
    {
      "id": "story-003",
      "title": "A Little House for a Hamster",
      "titleZh": "给仓鼠的小房子",
      "intro": "Miller had a **dream** about a **brave** **hamster** in a tiny house.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "title": "A dream house",
          "image": "story-003-scene-01.png",
          "english": "Miller had a **dream** about a **brave** **hamster** in a tiny house.\n\nIn the morning, Dad used a **saw** to build that house.\n\nMiller carried the pieces in a **basket**.",
          "translation": "Miller 梦见一只勇敢的仓鼠住在小房子里。早上，爸爸用锯子做这间房子，Miller 用篮子搬木块。",
          "labels": "dream, brave, hamster, saw, basket.",
          "days": "Day 15、Day 20"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "title": "A stuck basketball",
          "image": "story-003-scene-02.png",
          "english": "During a break, Miller tried to **shoot** a basketball into the hoop.\n\nThe ball got **stuck** under the garden workbench.\n\nHe **rang** Grandma to tell her about it.",
          "translation": "休息时，Miller 想投篮，但球卡在花园的工作台下面。他给奶奶打了电话，告诉她这件事。",
          "labels": "shoot, stuck, rang.",
          "days": "Day 16"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "title": "An odd little problem",
          "image": "story-003-scene-03.png",
          "english": "Miller **took** a long **rod** and a **net** to fetch the ball.\n\nA long **weed** was tangled in the net, and Miller felt **upset**.\n\n“That is **odd**!” he said.",
          "translation": "Miller 拿来一根长竿和一个网，想取出篮球。网里缠着一株长长的杂草，让他有点心烦。他说：“真奇怪！”",
          "labels": "took, rod, net, weed, upset, odd.",
          "days": "Day 17、Day 18"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "title": "Home at last",
          "image": "story-003-scene-04.png",
          "english": "Just then, the hamster **began** to run toward a hole in the fence.\n\nMiller shook the weed loose and **saved** the hamster with the net.\n\nThey put its **real** little house inside the **cage**.",
          "translation": "这时，仓鼠开始向栅栏上的洞跑去。Miller 抖掉网里的杂草，用网把仓鼠救了回来。最后，他们把真正做好的小房子放进笼子里。",
          "labels": "began, saved, real, cage.",
          "days": "Day 19、Day 20"
        }
      ],
      "week": 3,
      "startDay": 15,
      "endDay": 20,
      "entryCount": 18,
      "sceneCount": 4,
      "cover": "story-003-scene-01.png",
      "coverAlt": "A dream house",
      "hasPdf": false
    },
    {
      "id": "story-004",
      "title": "The Market and the Seaside Circus",
      "titleZh": "集市和海边马戏团",
      "intro": "A week **ago**, Miller **stood** on the **curb** beside his toy **wagon**.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "title": "An onion on the run",
          "image": "story-004-scene-01.png",
          "english": "A week **ago**, Miller **stood** on the **curb** beside his toy **wagon**.\n\nIt was full of **onions** for the market.\n\nA loose onion rolled away, so Miller had to **chase** it.",
          "translation": "一周以前，Miller 站在马路牙子上，旁边是装着洋葱的玩具四轮车。一只洋葱滚走了，他赶紧追了过去。",
          "labels": "ago, stood, curb, wagon, onions, chase.",
          "days": "Day 21、Day 22"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "title": "Seeds and a snack",
          "image": "story-004-scene-02.png",
          "english": "At the market, a farmer **sold** Miller some cheese shaped like a **cube**.\n\nShe gave him a **shovel** and **another** packet of seeds.\n\n“Let us **grow** some onions,” she said.",
          "translation": "在集市上，一位农场主卖给 Miller 一块立方体形状的奶酪，又给了他一把铲子和另一包种子。她说：“我们种些洋葱吧。”",
          "labels": "sold, cube, shovel, another, grow.",
          "days": "Day 22、Day 23"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "title": "A circus by the ocean",
          "image": "story-004-scene-03.png",
          "english": "They went to a **circus** on a piece of **land** beside the **ocean**.\n\nA **paddler** splashed through the shallow water.\n\nMiller made a **mistake** and left his ticket in the wagon.",
          "translation": "他们来到海边一块土地上的马戏团。一位涉水者在浅水中踩出了水花。Miller 发现自己犯了个错误：把票留在四轮车里了。",
          "labels": "circus, land, ocean, paddler, mistake.",
          "days": "Day 21、Day 24"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "title": "Waiting with Dad",
          "image": "story-004-scene-04.png",
          "english": "An **ordered** row of chairs stood **along** the path.\n\n“Do not wait here **alone**,” Grandma said.\n\n“I **care** about you, so stay with Dad.”",
          "translation": "小路旁的椅子排得整整齐齐。奶奶去取票前说：“不要独自在这里等。我关心你，所以和爸爸待在一起。”",
          "labels": "ordered, along, alone, care.",
          "days": "Day 25"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "title": "A heavy trunk",
          "image": "story-004-scene-05.png",
          "english": "Miller saw a new **type** of **van** with a **heavy** **trunk** in the back.\n\n“Let us **weigh** it **once** more,” Dad said, while Miller read the **scale** on the dial.\n\nThey hoped to **reach** home before dinner.",
          "translation": "Miller 看见一种新的客货车，车后放着一个沉重的行李箱。爸爸说：“我们再称一次吧。”Miller 看着秤的表盘上的刻度。他们希望晚饭前到家。",
          "labels": "type, van, heavy, trunk, weigh, once, scale, reach.",
          "days": "Day 26、Day 27"
        }
      ],
      "week": 4,
      "startDay": 21,
      "endDay": 27,
      "entryCount": 28,
      "sceneCount": 5,
      "cover": "story-004-scene-01.png",
      "coverAlt": "An onion on the run",
      "hasPdf": false
    },
    {
      "id": "story-005",
      "title": "A Kind Day at the Farm",
      "titleZh": "农场里友善的一天",
      "intro": "“You are an **honest** **person**,” the farmer said when Miller returned a lost coin.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "title": "An honest person",
          "image": "story-005-scene-01.png",
          "english": "“You are an **honest** **person**,” the farmer said when Miller returned a lost coin.\n\nThen Miller bought some **peanuts** with his own money.",
          "translation": "Miller 把捡到的硬币还给农场主，农场主夸他是个诚实的人。然后，Miller 用自己的钱买了些花生。",
          "labels": "honest, person, peanuts.",
          "days": "Day 28"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "title": "A living being",
          "image": "story-005-scene-02.png",
          "english": "Beside the shop, Miller watched a **goldfish** swim.\n\nA sign said, “Every living **being** needs food and water.”\n\n“What **else** does it need?” he asked.",
          "translation": "小店旁，Miller 看着金鱼游动。牌子上写着：“每一个有生命的个体都需要食物和水。”他问：“它还需要什么呢？”",
          "labels": "goldfish, being, else.",
          "days": "Day 28、Day 29"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "title": "Giddyup!",
          "image": "story-005-scene-03.png",
          "english": "There was a pile of **hay** beside a wooden horse.\n\n“Let us **pretend** it can run,” Miller said.\n\n“**Giddyup**!” he called from the saddle.",
          "translation": "木马旁有一堆干草。Miller 说：“我们假装它能跑吧。”他坐在马鞍上喊：“驾！”",
          "labels": "hay, pretend, Giddyup.",
          "days": "Day 29、Day 30"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "title": "One last game",
          "image": "story-005-scene-04.png",
          "english": "Behind a low **fence**, Miller found a **swing** and a **seesaw**.\n\nHe tried them both before going home.",
          "translation": "矮栅栏后面有一个秋千和一个跷跷板。Miller 都玩了一会儿，然后回家了。",
          "labels": "fence, swing, seesaw.",
          "days": "Day 30"
        }
      ],
